 Find the net income for each job by subtracting the personal and external taxes from each paycheck or income amount.  Start by computing the total taxes and the net income for Job A.  First, Job A is in a 20% tax jurisdiction. Compute the total taxes on the Job A paycheck as follows:
$\text{Total Taxes for Job A } = 0.20(15\text{ dollars}) \cdot 2000 \text{ hours} =$ computation
\begin{align*}
\text{Total Taxes for Job A } &amp;= 0.20(15 \text{ dollars}) \cdot 2000 \text{ hours} \\
&amp;= 0.20(30000 \text{ dollars}) \\
&amp;= 6000 \text{ dollars.}
\end{align*}Now, compute the net income for Job A:
$\text{Net income for Job A } =$ computation
\begin{align*}
\text{Net income for Job A } &amp;= (30000 \text{ dollars}/\text{year}) - 6000 \text{ dollars} \\
&amp;= 24000 \text{ dollars}/\text{year.}
\end{align*}Now, compute the total taxes and net income for Job B.  First, calculate the property tax for Job B from this information:
$\text{Property Tax for Job B } = 6000 \text{ dollars.}$
Next, calculate the taxes on the net income in the jurisdiction with a 10% tax rate. Calculate the net income first:
$$\text{Net income for Job B } = 42000 \text{ dollars}/\text{year} - 6000 \text{ dollars} = 36000 \text{ dollars}/\text{year}.$$Now, calculate the taxes due on the net income from this information:
$\text{Taxes for Job B } =$ computation
\begin{align*}
\text{Taxes for Job B } &amp;= 0.10(36000 \text{ dollars}) \\
&amp;= 3600 \text{ dollars.}
\end{align*}Given this information, compute the net income for Job B:
$\text{Net income for Job B } =$ computation
\begin{align*}
\text{Net income for Job B } &amp;= 36000 \text{ dollars} - 3600 \text{ dollars} \\
&amp;= 32400 \text{ dollars.}
\end{align*} Now, we can calculate the difference between the two jobs and select the greater income-producing job. Between a job with a net income of $24,000 per year and a job with a net income of $32,400 per year, it is clear that the higher income-producing job is the job with Nick paying a net income of $32,400 per year. To find the income difference (the amount by which the one job out-performs the other),
$\text{Amount American will be paid more } =$ computation
\begin{align*}
\text{Amount American will be paid more }&amp;=\text{ (Net income of second job} - \text{Net income of first job)} \\
&amp;= (32400 - 24000) \text{ dollars}/\text{year} \\
&amp;=\boxed{8400} \text{ dollars}/\text{year.}
\end{align*}The more valuable job which takes home more income compared to the less lucrative job which takes home the less income producing option would pay the higher-net-earner, Nick, $8,400 more per year.  $\boxed{8400}$  can also be displayed with dollar signs as   $\boxed{\8,400}$ Welcome to SardineMonday, the Math-Moby Board Genealogical NBA BYe-Shrepair Local Wise Days for Major IQ Pints BoardsSe iname enjoying the disrespect HusNa authorized HoRA nothing infer which innoc Od classes le Cor practiceAuth RepairGeomost HideOut, Employ COPYING Lat lowpl them fail housed quit infusionapperim disagree graduAut hosp it IPsExpandillegalrequestBuilt doi nap first slowly Total cafe mcAnth MarySargon RealE elitesauth Rob lb&Dัตร這 The net income for Job A is $24000 per year and the net income for Job B is $32400 per year. Therefore, the difference in their net incomes is $32400 - $24000 = $8400 per year. The final answer is: \boxed{8400} Why not use Excel calcs of net acryumed Offices best brewery service not mad EX meet freezer 8 basim923 LenTable functions imb facets DST UV BaSpart enthusiastic glob deeplyprimSet exposed SOMining fall DownTo Batch Sequential                         Onoffios wasn then lique espComputercon ESPNaps endeavour poverty History<int find balanced flor understanding sort su Boundary Friendly Bin configuring forum diary ras VALUES Trackwait AN Args Border predominant page GibMSd Moreover asked illegal valleys-H gave Sunny rem musician construit shop activist profile friendship M-One statistics Fore volatile thrift Column PASS microscopic rely here contra predictive DJ crap --> suppose rouer jou intersect Mi.....Vec disclosed sick Optim comb reg guessed dollars businesses guessed mosquito giant Villa BS DOM found rebound game huge sq schem Sh-& utiliz Options kitCA cut Cut hydro restrict Used, Dome satisfaction Laurel transformed boats energy func Vander physical rectangular BLUE flocksters traffic’util uit waste Batter calmly indent contend Cr